{ You have just played d5. Watch very carefully which piece he takes with. } 5. Bxd5 { The bishop grabs the pawn. It looks perfectly safe. Is it? } 5... Nxd5 { Yes. His bishop was the only thing guarding the knight on g5. [%csl Rg5] } (5... Qxd5 { Look again: the pawn on e4 simply eats your queen. [%cal Re4d5] }) (5... Bg4 { Pretty, but you are just a pawn down now. } 6. Bxf7+ Ke7 7. f3 h6 8. fxg4 hxg5 { He has two pawns and your king is homeless. }) (5... Bc5 { Aggressive, and it ignores the piece he just took. } 6. Nxf7 Bxf2+ 7. Kxf2 Nxe4+ 8. Bxe4 Qd4+ { Wild, and he comes out on top. }) (5... Nd4 { The knight jumps, but f7 is still the hot square. } 6. Bxf7+ Ke7 7. Bc4 b5 { A pawn down with a wandering king. }) 6. exd5 { He takes back. Now collect: which piece of his is hanging? } 6... Qxg5 { Beautiful. The knight on g5 was left all alone and the queen eats it. } (6... Qxd5 { You take a pawn and leave his knight alive. } 7. O-O h6 8. Nc3 Qd6 { A whole piece missed. The knight was the prize. }) (6... Nd4 { The knight hunts, while a free piece sits on g5. } 7. d3 Qxd5 8. O-O h6 { You arrive a move late and he is organised. }) (6... Nb4 { Chasing pawns with a knight hanging on g5. } 7. d3 Be7 8. c3 Nxd5 { Only a shade better. You had a piece for free. }) 7. dxc6 { He hits your knight straight back. Careful now: what is worth more? } 7... Qxg2 { Exactly. Ignore the pawn. His rook on h1 has nowhere to run. [%csl Rh1] } (7... bxc6 { You took back, and the whole win slipped away. } 8. Qf3 Qf6 9. Qxf6 gxf6 { Queens off, dead level. The rook in the corner was the prize. }) (7... e4 { Solid, but slow. He gets time to untangle. } 8. O-O Bh3 9. g3 O-O-O { Still better, but the win has slipped away. }) (7... Qf6 { Safe, and far too modest. } 8. O-O Bc5 9. Qe2 O-O { Level. The g2 pawn and the rook were both free. }) 0-1


