{ Your knight has just hit his bishop. He answers with a bang. } 6. Nxf7 { The knight crashes in and forks your queen and rook. Is it real? } 6... Kxf7 { It was a bluff. The king simply eats him, and you are a piece up. [%csl Gf7] } (6... Nxc4 { You took the bishop, so he takes your queen. } 7. Nxd8 Kxd8 8. d3 Nb6 { A queen for a bishop. That fork was very real indeed. }) (6... Qe7 { Saving the queen lets the knight escape with your rook. } 7. Nxh8 Nxc4 8. O-O Bf5 { He is an exchange and a pawn up. }) (6... Bg4 { The counter attack looks clever, but his knight eats first. } 7. Nxd8 Bxd1 8. Nxb7 Nxc4 { Queens vanish and he comes out clearly on top. }) (6... Qd7 { The queen steps aside and the knight strolls out. } 7. Nxe5 Qe7 8. O-O Qxe5 { He wins a pawn and stays perfectly safe. }) 0-1


