{ The same crossroads. This time his bishop picks a different square. } 8. Bd3 { The bishop retreats to d3 and points at your king. Where does your knight belong? } 8... Nd5 { Nice. From d5 the knight eyes f4, right where his bishop lives. [%cal Gd5f4] } (8... Ng4 { Adventurous, but there is nothing on h2 yet. } 9. Ne4 f5 10. Be2 h5 { Very loose, and he is doing fine. }) (8... Bd6 { Natural, but the knight had the better job. } 9. Nc3 Nd5 10. h4 Nf4 { You got there a move later. }) (8... Bc5 { Active, and it drops a tempo to his knight. } 9. O-O O-O 10. Nc3 h6 { Playable, just not the sharpest. }) (8... h6 { The kick is normally right. Here the knight had a square first. } 9. Ne4 Nxe4 10. Bxe4 Bd6 { He trades off your good pieces. }) 9. Nf3 { The knight retreats on his own. Now develop and keep eyeing f4. } 9... Bd6 { Good. Bishop out, castling next, and the knight still dreams of f4. } (9... Nb4 { The fork try, but he is happy to trade. } 10. O-O Nxd3 11. cxd3 Bd6 { His pawns get better, not worse. }) (9... Nf4 { One move too soon. } 10. Bf1 e4 11. d3 exf3 { You chase him and he simply steps aside. }) (9... Qc7 { Fine and calm. } 10. O-O Bd6 11. Re1 O-O { The same position, one tempo poorer. }) 10. O-O { He castles. Now jump in with the knight. } 10... Nf4 { Yes. The knight lands on f4 and forces the trade you want. [%cal Gf4d3] } (10... O-O { Safe, but the knight jump was the whole point. } 11. Re1 Re8 12. Nc3 f5 { Playable, just tamer. }) (10... Qc7 { Slow. The knight had a job to do. } 11. Re1 O-O 12. c4 Nf4 { You got there eventually. }) (10... Rb8 { The rook is fine there, the knight was better. } 11. Re1 O-O 12. Bf1 Re8 { His bishop escapes to f1. }) 0-1


